course: dictionary
lesson: 5210
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Look at the words around it and at any capital letters. «Jasmine blamed the last cookie on her sister, then the dog, then «maybe it just fell».» Jasmine has a capital letter and is a person's name, so it is not a plant here.
explain: The same word can name a plant, a food and a person. Jasmine can be a climbing bush with sweet white or yellow flowers. Jasmine tea is green tea flavoured with those flowers, and jasmine rice is a long rice that smells sweet. Try each meaning in the sentence and keep the one that fits.
explain: A capital letter often tells you a word is a name. Jasmine is a girl's name, so it is a proper noun. In «Jasmine asks Lucy to paint her nails», the capital J and the words asks and her show that Jasmine is a person doing something.
fact: Jasmine is a climbing plant or bush with small white or yellow flowers.
fact: The flowers of jasmine smell very sweet, and they attract moths and bees at night.
fact: «Jasmine tea» is green tea flavoured with jasmine flowers.
fact: «Jasmine rice» is a sweet-smelling kind of long rice.
fact: Jasmine is also a girl's name, and it always starts with a capital letter: «Jasmine».
exercise: «Jasmine blamed the last cookie on her sister.» Who or what is Jasmine in this sentence? | *A girl's name, a person | A kind of rice | A cup of green tea | A plant with white flowers
exercise: What is jasmine rice? | *A long, sweet-smelling kind of rice | A climbing plant with white flowers | A sort of bread | A girl in a story
exercise: «The wall was covered in jasmine, and its flowers smelt sweet.» What does jasmine mean here? | A kind of tea | A type of bird | A person's name | *A climbing plant with sweet-smelling flowers
test: «Jasmine asks Lucy to paint her nails.» Is Jasmine a plant or a person here? | A bee | A plant | A cup of tea | *A person
test: Moths and bees come to jasmine at night. What draws them to it? | *Its sweet scent | Its bright red colour | Its loud noise | Its heavy roots
exam: «She poured a cup of jasmine tea after dinner.» Which meaning of jasmine fits here? | A climbing plant on a wall | A girl's name | *Green tea flavoured with jasmine flowers | A bee's nest
